% ============================================================================
% phoneme-blending.query.adj — a worked recall over the literacy
% phoneme-blending library.
% ============================================================================
% The shape a learner (or an LLM) produces to ANSWER "what word do /s/, /o/,
% and /p/ blend into?": it states no linguistics fact — it only `import`s the
% grounded table and asks binding queries. The engine resolves each `?`
% against the `phoneme_blending` rows and returns the word + the table's
% source/locator/trust. The second query runs the relation BACKWARD (bind the
% word `soap`, recall the three sounds that blend into it). A sound triple
% this source does not demonstrate blending is not in the table, so a recall
% on it abstains honestly — the engine never invents a blend.
%
% Run (from this directory so the relative import resolves):
%     ../../../../packages/rust/target/debug/adj-lang-cli phoneme-blending.query.adj
% ============================================================================

import "phoneme-blending.adj"

? phoneme_blending(s, o, p, $Word)          % expect soap
? phoneme_blending($S1, $S2, $S3, soap)     % expect s, o, p — reverse recall
? phoneme_blending(b, a, t, $Word)          % expect abstain — not the blend this source demonstrates
